<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>Uncle Mark's Tutorials - 1 - NATO Surface Group vs. Soviet Forces, 1985</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;Welcome!&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;My name is Mark Gellis.&amp;nbsp; I am not officially associated with Matrix Games or Warfare Sims, but I enjoy Command, and I enjoy writing scenarios for it.&amp;nbsp; This is part of my ongoing effort to help those who are new to Command learn the game so they can get the most enjoyment out of it.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This scenario is a very basic Cold War battle.&amp;nbsp; It assumes World War III has started in 1985, and that you are in charge of a small surface action group (SAG).&amp;nbsp; Your job is to hunt Soviet ships and submarines and destroy them before they can get out into the Atlantic ocean, where they could threaten NATO convoys.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Your forces consist of three warships--a British destroyer, a Dutch frigate, and a German frigate.&amp;nbsp; You also have&amp;nbsp;three helicopters for scouting the seas ahead of your ships and for hunting submarines.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As always, I've included an .ini file in the .zip file for this scenario that can be used to update this scenario to future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; You don't have to do anything with it right now; it is there if you need it in the future.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Enjoy the scenario!&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
